# TypeScript Conventions

## Strict Mode

- `strict: true` in tsconfig — no shortcuts
- No `any` — prefer `unknown` and narrow with type guards
- `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`, `noImplicitReturns` enabled

## Types

- Use string literal unions for finite state sets:
  ```typescript
  type BumpType = 'major' | 'minor' | 'patch' | 'none';
  type TagStrategy = 'full' | 'all' | 'full-and-minor';
  type LlmProvider = 'openai' | 'anthropic' | 'openrouter';
  ```
- Use `satisfies` for type-safe const objects
- Use `Record<K, V>` for exhaustive mappings
- Validate all external input at boundaries (action inputs, API responses, file reads)

## Functions

- Explicit return types on exported functions
- Prefer pure functions — isolate side effects (API calls, I/O)
- Use `async/await` over raw promises
- Early returns for guard clauses

## Testing

- Mock external dependencies (`@actions/core`, `@actions/github`, `fetch`)
- Test edge cases: empty input, missing tags, API errors, malformed data
- Each test file mirrors its source module
